## Guard and evidence boundary

The outer script checks all 154 pinned inputs, then under the existing activation lock loads each pinned role plan and rejects its exact profile path if it exists or is a symlink. It records the guarded paths and `allAbsentBeforeActivation: true` before activating source files. The only script/plan changes from the preserved unexecuted proposal are this guard, the new outer-script pin, and matching launch bindings. At review time, the profile path and C/native outputs are absent.

All 154 outer pins match. SOURCE02 freeze/archive hashes match; the 53-file inventory matches the native plan, with five intentional activated files backed up exactly and the other 48 unchanged. The native plan’s only five preactivation hash differences are those activation bodies and are checked after activation by the existing delivery/source-boundary preflights. The outer activation lock is distinct from the collector’s heavy lock; its `finally` restores and verifies all 53 source entries.

The pinned sidearchive (`12b98d5a844d580c014177cc797d58e5626b3a6d4d5f7e82c9781264b3d772cb`) contains byte-identical preserved profiled source, exit status 77, summary, and a parseable nonempty CPU profile with 17,541 samples. It supports the cooperative-stop/profile-flush method, not this candidate’s future result.

The expected diagnostic exit 77 makes the unchanged collector receipt `INCOMPLETE`. A long synchronous definition/postwork step or profile flush can miss the cooperative boundary and outer 30-second cap, leaving the profile missing; classify that as defined diagnostic failure. After terminal status and source restoration, final review must hash and parse the profile before using it, distinguishing valid nonempty samples, missing output, and invalid/empty JSON. CPU/RSS/heap-used boundaries and sampled CPU stacks do not establish an allocation timeline, peak memory, or performance improvement. The run uses the frozen 53-source scope, CPU 3, caps 30/120/5, and pinned 207,834-byte oracle, but exit 77 provides no C/build/consumer result or native credit.
